MARS(1)                         User Commands                         MARS(1)

NAME
     mars - minimal single-instrument latent-state trading research engine

SYNOPSIS
     make
     make install

     mars inspect model.mars
     mars fit-db market.db model.mars [table]
     mars replay-db market.db model.mars trades.csv [table]

     mars db-init market.db
     mars db-summary market.db
     mars eth-update market.db FROM_BLOCK TO_BLOCK [--blocks-only]
     mars eth-export market.db ethblocks.csv
     mars dex-update market.db FROM_BLOCK TO_BLOCK [POOL]
     mars dex-export market.db dexswaps.csv [POOL]
     mars fred-update market.db SERIES[,SERIES...]
     mars fred-export market.db fred.csv

DESCRIPTION
     mars is a small research engine for fitting, inspecting, and replaying a
     latent-state trading model for one instrument at a time.

     The intended first instrument is CME ES/MES 1-second top-of-book bars.

FILES
     src/main.c
          Plain C command entrypoint and argument dispatch.

     src/api.h
          C-compatible boundary, status codes, constants, and shared POD
          model/data types.

     src/core.cpp
          C++ orchestration over focused module classes.

     src/data.cpp, src/data.hpp
          data: load market bars directly from SQLite.

     src/features.cpp, src/features.hpp
          features: construct model features from market rows.

     src/scale.cpp, src/scale.hpp
          scale: fit/apply scalers and build feature matrices.

     src/hmm.cpp, src/hmm.hpp
          hmm: fit and filter latent states.

     src/alpha.cpp, src/alpha.hpp
          alpha: train and apply the sparse alpha model.

     src/backtest.cpp, src/backtest.hpp
          backtest: replay predictions into PnL and trade output.

     src/store.cpp, src/store.hpp
          store: default config, validation, save, and load.

     src/report.cpp, src/report.hpp
          report: stats and model inspection output.

     src/db.cpp
          SQLite schema, Ethereum block ingestion, FRED ingestion, and summary
          commands.

     src/dex.cpp, src/dex.hpp
          dex: on-chain Uniswap V3 WETH/USDC swap ingestion and training view.

     Makefile
          Builds and installs mars. DB ingestion links against libcurl and
          sqlite3.

INPUT
     DB commands write local SQLite data. Training reads market bars directly
     from SQLite through fit-db and replay-db. If the default market_bars table
     is empty, fit-db and replay-db first use on-chain DEX WETH/USDC swaps when
     available, then fall back to a derived Ethereum base-fee series.
     mars does not fetch centralized-exchange ETH/USD candles; built-in ETH
     price rows are sourced from Ethereum JSON-RPC logs.

COMMANDS
     make
          Build the local binary at build/mars.

     make install
          Install mars to PREFIX/bin. PREFIX defaults to /usr/local.

     make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local
          Install mars to $HOME/.local/bin for a user-local setup.
          Ensure $HOME/.local/bin is in PATH to run mars by name.

     mars inspect es.mars
          Inspect learned latent states and sparse alpha coefficients.

     mars fit-db market.db es.mars
          Fit a model from market_bars, or from derived Ethereum chain data when
          market_bars is empty.

     mars fit-db market.db es.mars my_bars
          Fit directly from another table or view with the market-bar schema.

     mars replay-db market.db es.mars trades.csv
          Replay a fitted model from the same default DB source.

     Training knobs
          fit-db reads optional environment overrides for model assumptions:

               MARS_HORIZON
               MARS_TICK_SIZE
               MARS_TURN_COST
               MARS_EDGE_COST
               MARS_BUFFER
               MARS_MAX_SPREAD
               MARS_POS_MAX
               MARS_TURNOVER_PENALTY

          These are stored in the fitted model. replay-db uses the saved model
          values, so replay does not need the same environment variables.
          MARS_TURNOVER_PENALTY affects model selection only.

     mars db-init market.db
          Initialize the local SQLite learning database.

     mars db-summary market.db
          Print table counts, Ethereum/FRED date coverage, and the source that
          fit-db will train from by default.

     mars eth-update market.db FROM_BLOCK TO_BLOCK [--blocks-only]
          Fetch Ethereum block and optional transaction data using ETH_RPC_URL.

     mars eth-export market.db ethblocks.csv
          Export Ethereum block-level learning features.

     mars dex-update market.db FROM_BLOCK TO_BLOCK [POOL]
          Fetch on-chain Uniswap V3 swap logs using ETH_RPC_URL. The default
          pool is mainnet WETH/USDC 0.05%. Dense historical ranges can lower
          the JSON-RPC log window:

               MARS_DEX_BLOCK_BATCH=500 mars dex-update market.db 24000000 24100000

     mars dex-export market.db dexswaps.csv [POOL]
          Export stored DEX swap observations.

     mars fred-update market.db SERIES[,SERIES...]
          Fetch FRED observations using FRED_API_KEY.

     mars fred-export market.db fred.csv
          Export stored FRED observations.

DATABASE
     The local learning database is SQLite. Initialize it with:

          mars db-init market.db

     Market bars
          The model trains on top-of-book market bars shaped as:

               ts,bid,ask,bid_sz,ask_sz,volume

          The default SQLite table is market_bars. Populate that table directly
          with SQLite, or create a view with the same columns, then fit and
          replay directly from SQLite:

               mars fit-db market.db es.mars
               mars replay-db market.db es.mars trades.csv

          Any table or view with the same six columns can be used:

               mars fit-db market.db es.mars my_market_view

     Ethereum DEX bars
          When market_bars has fewer than the minimum training rows and no
          explicit table is supplied, mars first reads the dex_training_bars
          view. This trains an ETH spot-price movement model from on-chain
          WETH/USDC swaps, not centralized-exchange candles.

          The view derives one market-bar-shaped row per active minute from
          real Uniswap V3 Swap events. It uses the last swap price in that
          minute as the close, actual swap sizes as depth/volume inputs,
          Ethereum block fields when present, and FRED macro observations as-of
          the minute timestamp.

               export ETH_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
               mars dex-update market.db 19000000 19001000
               mars dex-update market.db 0 latest

          DEX tables:

               dex_swaps
               dex_training_bars

     Ethereum base-fee bars
          If neither market_bars nor dex_training_bars has enough rows, mars
          reads the basefee_training_bars view. This trains a base-fee movement
          model, not an ETH spot-price model.

          The view derives bid/ask-shaped rows from real eth_block_features:
          base_fee_gwei is scaled by 100 so sub-gwei moves fit the default tick
          model. Its default auxiliary features are Ethereum-chain fields and
          FRED macro observations as-of the block timestamp.

     Ethereum chain data
          mars talks to an Ethereum execution JSON-RPC endpoint and calls
          eth_getBlockByNumber. The default stores full transaction objects;
          --blocks-only stores real block headers and transaction counts without
          transaction-body aggregates. Run your own node if possible; hosted RPC
          endpoints work for small backfills but are usually rate-limited for
          large historical ingestion.

               export ETH_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
               mars eth-update market.db 19000000 19001000
               mars eth-update market.db 0 latest --blocks-only

          Ethereum tables:

               eth_blocks
               eth_txs
               eth_block_features
               dex_swaps
               dex_training_bars
               basefee_training_bars

          Block header fields are stored from JSON-RPC observations.
          Transaction-body aggregates in eth_block_features are NULL unless
          full transaction bodies have been ingested.

     FRED data
          FRED observations are fetched with FRED_API_KEY:

               export FRED_API_KEY=...
               mars fred-update market.db DGS2,DGS10,T10Y2Y,VIXCLS,DTWEXBGS,WALCL

          FRED tables:

               fred_series
               fred_observations

     Exports
          eth-export, dex-export, and fred-export are for inspection and
          interoperability. Export files are no longer part of the training
          path.

DESIGN
     Instrument choice
          ES/MES first, because it is centralized, liquid, tick-discrete,
          high-frequency enough to learn microstructure states, and avoids
          corporate actions, borrow, and fragmented equity NBBO reconstruction.

     Latent states
          Learned by causal diagonal-Gaussian HMM filtering. States are not
          manually named. Inspect state emission means after fitting.

     Alpha
          Regime-interacted elastic net. Rich enough to condition on latent
          regimes; sparse enough to avoid feature proliferation.

     Execution model
          One-unit position in {-1,0,+1}, hard spread guard, cost threshold,
          and validation gate. If validation is not positive after costs, the
          saved model is deployment-disabled with pos_max=0.

     Style
          Single binary, plain Makefile, C command surface, C++ core behind a
          small C ABI, deterministic replay, checked return values, no
          recursion, and bounded inner loops.

STATUS
     This is a research scaffold. It is not a broker adapter, not a live
     execution engine, and not a claim about Renaissance Technologies' actual
     code.
